        "created_at": "2025-08-04T15:10:35.318477+00:00",
        "notes": "Here comes the hard part for me. I reached Round 6 with this build a few times, but I never established what I wanted. I'll suggest a few options, and update this if anyone finds a good pick.\n\n [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6), or  [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) if you can spare the cash, is the best option for boosting ability power.\n\n [Divine Intervention](item_b5148b7f-8529-4b1b-a90c-5d7cf13f8f0c) is an extremely underrated item, and can save your life against  [Reinhardt](hero_a3b6ca2c-6cbd-43dc-bb78-a728e42fba49),  [Junkrat](hero_3ac20f6c-2bce-45f3-998e-9129cc6e5c05),  [Freja](hero_e80840a1-845d-4008-966c-585b7cb4a424) and many others, though it comes at the cost of less ability power.\n\n [Coalegion](item_ff9adeb1-362c-46a4-80ef-4e0eb07479cc) offers a damage boost during your ultimate, basically turning it into a long, thin version of Juno's Orbital Ray. While that ultimate is powerful in regular games, having played Juno a bit in Stadium, it's usefulness definitely decreases in later rounds.\n\n [Catalytic Crystal](item_3e3f4f77-cdf8-4dda-a5b0-2fb9390aefc4) allows you to get your ultimate up much faster. I avoided this later into my climb because it sometimes felt like using my ultimate *decreased* my healing output.",
